<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 18.56 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 18.56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 115 basis points to 18.56 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     19.71	    18.56		   -115 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     22.08	    20.83		   -125 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    23.18	    22.00		   -118 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     23.38	    23.38		   - 97 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830</p>
<p>(2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((--Elena Vega, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
